<P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"><STRONG><SPAN lang=EN-GB style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal; COLOR: black; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 7.0pt"><FONT face="arial, helvetica, sans-serif"><FONT size=1>Here’s what <STRONG>The Guardian</STRONG> had to say on 27th November:<o:p></o:p></FONT></FONT></SPAN></STRONG></P>
<P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"><STRONG><SPAN lang=EN-GB style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal; COLOR: black; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 7.0pt"><FONT face="arial, helvetica, sans-serif"><FONT size=1> <o:p></o:p></FONT></FONT></SPAN></STRONG></P>
<P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"><STRONG><SPAN lang=EN-GB style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal; COLOR: black; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 7.0pt"><FONT face="arial, helvetica, sans-serif"><FONT size=1> <o:p></o:p></FONT></FONT></SPAN></STRONG></P>
<P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"><FONT face="arial, helvetica, sans-serif"><FONT size=1><STRONG><SPAN lang=EN-GB style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal; COLOR: black; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 7.0pt">“<STRONG>Andrew</STRONG> is seriously interested to buy <STRONG>Warner Chappell</STRONG>. He’s rather hopeful to create a pool", as claimed by his </SPAN></STRONG><STRONG><SPAN lang=EN-US style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal; COLOR: black; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-font-size: 7.0pt">spokesperson</SPAN></STRONG><STRONG><SPAN lang=EN-GB style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal; COLOR: black; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 7.0pt">. <STRONG>The Guardian</STRONG> values the division around one billion dollars. <o:p></o:p></SPAN></STRONG></FONT></FONT></P>
<P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"><STRONG><SPAN lang=EN-GB style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal; COLOR: black; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 7.0pt"><FONT face="arial, helvetica, sans-serif"><FONT size=1> <o:p></o:p></FONT></FONT></SPAN></STRONG></P>
<P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"><STRONG><SPAN lang=EN-GB style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal; COLOR: black; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 7.0pt"><FONT face="arial, helvetica, sans-serif"><FONT size=1>The news arrives last Monday after <STRONG>Time Warner</STRONG> accepted to sell <STRONG>Warner Music</STRONG>, including authors like <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>, <STRONG>Led Zeppelin</STRONG> and <STRONG>Rem</STRONG>, to a group guided by <STRONG>Bronfman</STRONG> for 2,6 million dollars. The deal left out an offer valued around one billion dollars by <STRONG>Emi group</STRONG>. <STRONG>Bronfman</STRONG> was unreachable for any comments.<SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes">       </SPAN><o:p></o:p></FONT></FONT></SPAN></STRONG></P>
